WEBVTT

00:00.960 --> 00:01.930
There it is again!

00:01.960 --> 00:04.300
Wha-- Where is it coming from?

00:04.330 --> 00:06.170
[BOTH gasp]

00:07.700 --> 00:10.140
[NARRATOR] Setting camp at
the ruins of Utgard Castle

00:10.170 --> 00:12.170
for the night,

00:12.210 --> 00:15.840
the Scouts found themselves
overtaken by a Titan horde.

00:15.950 --> 00:18.280
Their chances of survival low.

00:18.310 --> 00:20.450
[CHRISTA]
Nanaba. Gelgar.

00:20.480 --> 00:22.180
I'm sorry, Daddy!
I'll be a good girl

00:22.220 --> 00:23.780
from now on, I promise!

00:23.820 --> 00:25.890
[NARRATOR]
But when all seemed lost.

00:25.960 --> 00:28.060
[YMIR]
Listen to me.

00:28.120 --> 00:29.720
When you break it down,

00:29.790 --> 00:32.360
this is really
just more of a hope.

00:32.400 --> 00:36.730
Christa. Live a life
you can be proud of.

00:36.800 --> 00:39.130
[CHRISTA]
Ymir! Wait!

00:40.840 --> 00:44.440
[NARRATOR] One of their own
made a shocking transformation.

00:45.340 --> 00:47.670
Yeah! Atta girl!

00:49.210 --> 00:52.780
[YMIR TITAN]
Wanna live? Grab on tight.

00:58.990 --> 01:00.250
[CONNY]
That's not good.

01:00.320 --> 01:02.760
[Gasps]

01:02.830 --> 01:04.430
[CONNY]
They're eating her!

01:06.600 --> 01:10.660
[CHRISTA] No! I still
haven't told you my name!

01:10.700 --> 01:13.730
I promised you!

01:16.040 --> 01:17.770
[NARRATOR] The main force
of the Scout Regiment

01:17.840 --> 01:20.670
swooped in and
engaged the enemy.

01:20.710 --> 01:22.710
Die!

01:25.920 --> 01:28.620
[NARRATOR] The Titan assault
fell before their blades.

01:28.680 --> 01:30.580
[MIKASA yells]

01:32.290 --> 01:36.020
[NARRATOR] However, standing
on the wreckage of battle,

01:36.060 --> 01:37.720
Eren and the others
bore witness

01:37.760 --> 01:41.630
to a heartbreaking confession.

01:41.700 --> 01:44.260
[CHRISTA]
Ymir.

01:44.300 --> 01:47.400
Just as promised.

01:47.440 --> 01:49.940
My real name is Historia.

01:59.980 --> 02:04.990
♪ Opening Song

03:55.380 --> 03:59.150
That's it.
Bring it up slowly.

04:00.620 --> 04:03.250
Steady the ropes, please.

04:10.500 --> 04:12.000
[EREN]
What's the verdict?

04:12.030 --> 04:15.070
How bad a shape is Ymir in?

04:15.130 --> 04:17.570
[KEIJI] Well, she's missing
an arm and a leg.

04:17.640 --> 04:20.700
And her insides are scrambled.

04:20.740 --> 04:23.640
If she was normal,
she'd be a goner.

04:26.210 --> 04:28.310
[EREN]
Normal, huh?

04:33.720 --> 04:37.850
[REINER groans]

04:37.890 --> 04:40.160
[EREN]
Here, grab my hand.

04:40.190 --> 04:41.790
Thanks.

04:45.200 --> 04:47.000
[CHRISTA] Please,
you've got to believe me!

04:47.030 --> 04:48.530
I'm telling the truth!

04:48.570 --> 04:50.530
Ymir could've run away
any time she wanted!

04:50.570 --> 04:53.740
She chose to fight the
Titans to save our lives!

04:53.770 --> 04:55.410
She had nothing to gain
putting herself

04:55.440 --> 04:57.040
on the line like that.

04:57.080 --> 05:00.380
Doesn't that speak volumes
about where her loyalties are?

05:00.410 --> 05:02.580
She should have
told us before, yes.

05:02.620 --> 05:04.950
She had no right to keep
her power a secret.

05:05.020 --> 05:07.250
It's hard to look past how much
humankind might've gained

05:07.290 --> 05:10.250
from knowing what she's been
keeping to her self, but...

05:10.290 --> 05:12.460
I think... I think
she was just worried

05:12.520 --> 05:15.590
about what people
might do to her.

05:15.630 --> 05:18.230
Clearly her priorities
have changed now.

05:18.260 --> 05:21.230
This isn't nearly as
complicated as it looks.

05:21.270 --> 05:23.530
No one is closer
to Ymir than me,

05:23.570 --> 05:28.270
and there's no question in my
mind whose side she's on!

05:28.310 --> 05:30.310
Is that so?

05:30.380 --> 05:31.910
Well, under
the circumstances

05:31.940 --> 05:35.410
it certainly behooves us
to be friendly.

05:35.450 --> 05:37.080
Her priorities aside,

05:37.120 --> 05:39.250
I'll wager what she can
teach us about the enemy

05:39.290 --> 05:42.690
is beyond measure. Probably.

05:44.390 --> 05:47.920
Even so. You say this
isn't as complicated

05:47.960 --> 05:49.960
as it looks, but from
where I'm standing

05:50.000 --> 05:52.930
the world gets more
complicated by the hour.

05:55.800 --> 06:00.470
[HANGE] Oh, uh--Historia Reiss
you said your name was?

06:00.510 --> 06:02.910
I did. That's correct.

06:02.940 --> 06:07.140
[HANGE] Isn't Reiss the name
of a noble family?

06:07.180 --> 06:09.310
Yes, it is.

06:09.350 --> 06:11.280
Huh.

06:14.450 --> 06:18.320
Historia, nice to meet'cha.

06:18.360 --> 06:20.290
Thank you.

06:24.260 --> 06:25.760
[HANGE]
How's she doing?

06:25.800 --> 06:29.100
Comatose but stable.
The bleeding's stopped,

06:29.130 --> 06:34.440
though steam appears to be
coming out of her wounds.

06:34.470 --> 06:36.540
Best course of action
is taking her back to Trost

06:36.610 --> 06:39.510
where the poor girl can
get proper medical care.

06:39.550 --> 06:41.140
She's in your hands.

06:41.180 --> 06:42.910
Consider it done.

06:44.980 --> 06:48.790
Right, then.
On with our mission.

06:48.820 --> 06:51.460
Finding the hole
and patching it up.

07:04.200 --> 07:07.200
[REINER exhales]
Son of bitch.

07:07.240 --> 07:09.510
You okay over there, Reiner?

07:09.540 --> 07:11.540
[REINER]
Not by a long shot.

07:11.640 --> 07:14.680
Titan almost gnawed my arm off.

07:14.710 --> 07:20.650
Pathetic. All I could think
was "this it how I go."

07:28.060 --> 07:30.530
What else you s'posed
to think at time like that?

07:30.560 --> 07:31.930
You're only human.

07:32.000 --> 07:35.270
Don't you get it?
This was my second time!

07:35.330 --> 07:36.730
Armin! Remember?

07:36.770 --> 07:38.000
Huh?

07:38.040 --> 07:39.400
[REINER]
Go on!

07:39.440 --> 07:42.440
Tell him how Annie nearly
crushed me like an insect!

07:46.010 --> 07:48.080
[ARMIN]
Yeah.

07:48.110 --> 07:51.110
That's twice
I've nearly died now.

07:51.180 --> 07:54.790
What are the chances
I'll survive a third time?

07:54.850 --> 07:56.850
This is what it really means.

07:56.890 --> 08:00.060
What it is to be soldier.

08:00.090 --> 08:04.360
Your spirit breaks
and the body follows.

08:05.260 --> 08:08.630
Eh. No good
whining about it now.

08:08.700 --> 08:11.400
'Least not till we can
plug up the wall.

08:11.440 --> 08:14.270
That's true. The two
of you have been driven

08:14.310 --> 08:16.870
far enough away from
your hometown as it is.

08:16.910 --> 08:18.940
--[REINER gasps]
--This is it.

08:18.980 --> 08:21.710
This is where
we draw the line.

08:23.220 --> 08:25.380
[BERTHOLDT] Truer words
were never spoken!

08:25.420 --> 08:30.390
Home! Let's go!
We've been here long enough!

08:30.420 --> 08:31.720
Compared to everything
else we've had

08:31.760 --> 08:35.630
to go through,
the rest is easy!

08:35.660 --> 08:37.230
You're right.

08:37.260 --> 08:40.960
We don't have much further
to go before it's done!

08:43.070 --> 08:46.440
[EREN]
What are guys talking about?

08:50.180 --> 08:52.240
I needed that. Thanks.

08:52.280 --> 08:53.640
Are you injured?

08:53.680 --> 08:57.110
Nah, I'm okay,
but, Reiner's wounded.

08:57.150 --> 09:00.780
And Ymir's sure
seen better days.

09:00.820 --> 09:03.790
[SASHA] Who would've ever
pegged her for a Titan?

09:03.820 --> 09:06.360
--Are they?
--[MIKASA] Sasha.

09:06.430 --> 09:08.260
[HANGE]
We all on the same page?

09:08.290 --> 09:10.360
We'll decide what to do
with Ymir later.

09:10.430 --> 09:12.600
Oh, and Conny?

09:12.630 --> 09:16.300
Chin up. I'll order a squad
to investigate your village.

09:16.340 --> 09:17.970
For now, stay focused.

09:18.000 --> 09:21.540
I want our energy on
the task at hand. Clear?

09:21.610 --> 09:24.140
Crystal!

09:24.180 --> 09:25.540
[HANGE]
It's troubling.

09:25.610 --> 09:28.910
You would expect this area
to be teeming with Titans.

09:28.950 --> 09:30.510
Hm?

09:31.980 --> 09:33.680
[SASHA]
Hannes?

09:33.720 --> 09:36.020
Is that the
Garrison advance squad?

09:36.090 --> 09:38.820
Tell me they've
located the breach.

09:45.830 --> 09:48.370
Wall's perfectly fine.

09:48.400 --> 09:49.670
What?

09:49.700 --> 09:51.130
[HANNES] Spent all night
trying to find out

09:51.170 --> 09:52.640
where they're getting in.

09:52.670 --> 09:55.740
But between Trost and Krolva
District, there's nothing.

09:55.810 --> 09:57.070
No hole anywhere.

09:57.140 --> 09:58.740
That's impossible!

09:58.810 --> 10:00.880
We ran into a
search party from Krolva

10:00.980 --> 10:02.680
and retraced our steps.

10:02.710 --> 10:06.320
Not a single Titan
on the way here either.

10:06.350 --> 10:08.990
[ARMIN] But we know for a fact
that there are Titans

10:09.020 --> 10:10.720
on this side of Wall Rose.

10:10.820 --> 10:11.920
Oh, C'mon.

10:11.990 --> 10:14.060
How much have you
had to drink, seriously?

10:14.090 --> 10:15.190
Why you little!

10:15.230 --> 10:16.430
Hold on, wait a second.

10:16.500 --> 10:18.900
What the hell are
you kids even doing here?

10:28.910 --> 10:29.940
If there's no breach,

10:30.010 --> 10:31.910
then I guess we
have to change tactics.

10:31.940 --> 10:34.840
We head back
to Trost immediately.

10:40.420 --> 10:44.550
You'd be smart
to keep your guard up.

10:44.590 --> 10:46.890
We'll go on ahead of you.

10:51.100 --> 10:53.960
How can there be
nothing wrong with the wall?

10:54.030 --> 10:56.470
[ARMIN]
Excellent question.

10:56.540 --> 10:58.970
Nothing like this
has happened in five years.

10:59.040 --> 11:01.240
Why now all of a sudden?

11:01.270 --> 11:04.070
[SASHA] Feels like everything's
spiraling out of control.

11:04.110 --> 11:06.280
[REINER]
Eren.

11:06.310 --> 11:10.210
We should talk.
You got a moment?

11:10.250 --> 11:12.820
Sure, I guess.

11:12.880 --> 11:15.790
[REINER] Five years ago,
we compromised Wall Maria

11:15.820 --> 11:18.090
and launched
an attack on humanity.

11:18.120 --> 11:20.490
Oh no. What if there's
a species of Titan

11:20.560 --> 11:22.730
we haven't seen yet
that knows how to dig?

11:22.760 --> 11:24.260
Ugh. That would
definitely make

11:24.300 --> 11:25.930
their entry point hard to find.

11:25.960 --> 11:29.000
[REINER] I'm the Armored Titan.
He's the Colossal.

11:29.070 --> 11:30.770
[HANGE]
We can hypothesize later.

11:30.800 --> 11:33.070
Our first concern is Ymir.

11:33.110 --> 11:36.770
[MOBLIT] Titans being a close
second, even with the horses.

11:38.540 --> 11:40.080
What are you talking about?

11:40.110 --> 11:42.410
Why are you telling him?
Reiner, no!

11:42.450 --> 11:43.810
--Stop!
--We were on a mission.

11:43.850 --> 11:47.450
Our goal was to ensure
mankind's extinction.

11:47.490 --> 11:51.420
But now,
there's no need for that.

11:51.460 --> 11:55.290
Eren, if you want the
walls to remain standing,

11:55.330 --> 11:59.600
it's simple. Just come
with Bertholdt and me.

11:59.630 --> 12:01.500
Do you understand?

12:01.530 --> 12:04.530
Understand? What the hell
is there to understand?

12:04.600 --> 12:08.970
[REINER] Listen to me. I need
you to do exactly as I say.

12:22.480 --> 12:25.350
[REINER] Look, I know this is
sudden, but we have to go.

12:25.380 --> 12:28.490
Right now?
Where would you take me?

12:28.520 --> 12:31.960
I can't tell you. Not yet.

12:31.990 --> 12:35.390
Just think of it
as our hometown.

12:35.460 --> 12:37.730
Okay? So what's it gonna be?

12:37.800 --> 12:39.030
[Gasps]

12:39.070 --> 12:40.700
[REINER]
Not a bad deal, right?

12:40.730 --> 12:43.130
The chance to avert
a major crisis?

12:45.140 --> 12:47.470
I'm not so sure.

12:47.510 --> 12:51.040
You guys! Get a move on,
we're heading out!

12:56.220 --> 12:58.980
[EREN] Damn it.
I didn't want to believe

12:59.020 --> 13:01.990
what I was hearing yesterday.

13:07.990 --> 13:10.560
[Horse neighs]

13:10.630 --> 13:12.160
[HANGE]
Hmmm.

13:12.200 --> 13:15.370
[EREN] Section Commander?
Something wrong?

13:15.400 --> 13:18.370
Uh--Huh? Oh, uh,
well I was finally able

13:18.400 --> 13:20.040
to get my hands on
the background report

13:20.070 --> 13:23.770
I requested for Annie Leonhart.

13:23.840 --> 13:25.240
Annie?

13:25.280 --> 13:28.850
[HANGE] Yeah. Took longer
than I was hoping for.

13:28.880 --> 13:31.850
The paper trail's a bit of
a catastrophe at the moment.

13:31.880 --> 13:33.850
Bureaucracy, huh?

13:33.890 --> 13:36.450
Anyway, according to this,
there were two other cadets

13:36.520 --> 13:40.090
in the 104th who haled
from the same region.

13:41.960 --> 13:44.290
I have their names.

13:44.360 --> 13:48.430
One Reiner Braun
and Bertholdt Hoover.

13:48.470 --> 13:50.530
[Gasps]

13:50.570 --> 13:52.540
[Gasps]

13:55.110 --> 13:57.740
Not much survives
in the way of records,

13:57.780 --> 13:59.710
and thanks to the chaos
five years ago,

13:59.750 --> 14:02.280
what we have on them
is unreliable.

14:02.310 --> 14:05.950
However, we do know
that during the long-range

14:05.990 --> 14:09.390
scouting formation, their
unit was given false intel.

14:09.420 --> 14:11.890
They were among those
intentionally misled into

14:11.920 --> 14:14.730
thinking Eren
was in the right wing.

14:15.900 --> 14:17.660
[Gasps]
Wait just a minute.

14:17.730 --> 14:19.930
That's the section
Annie attacked.

14:19.970 --> 14:22.070
[SASHA]
What? What does that mean?

14:22.100 --> 14:24.740
Well, it's entirely
possible they told Annie

14:24.770 --> 14:26.400
where they thought Eren was.

14:26.440 --> 14:28.240
Huh? Why would they do that?

14:28.270 --> 14:30.070
Where are you
going with this, Armin?

14:30.110 --> 14:31.310
You can't just accuse--!

14:31.340 --> 14:32.910
[HANGE]
I totally agree.

14:32.950 --> 14:37.250
Coincidence doesn't
establish relationship.

14:37.280 --> 14:39.180
Bearing that in mind,
I'm curious to know

14:39.250 --> 14:41.820
how the three interacted
while training.

14:41.850 --> 14:44.820
What can you tell me?

14:44.860 --> 14:47.290
I knew Bertholdt and Reiner
were from the same region

14:47.330 --> 14:51.090
as Annie, but I never
saw them act friendly.

14:51.130 --> 14:52.430
Same with me.

14:52.460 --> 14:54.360
You'd never catch 'em
shootin' the breeze.

14:54.430 --> 14:57.300
And when they did talk
it was pretty curt.

14:57.340 --> 15:01.000
Plus, it's not like Annie was
very social to begin with.

15:01.040 --> 15:03.510
Yeah, at meals
she always seemed to prefer

15:03.540 --> 15:06.010
eating by herself. I dunno.

15:06.050 --> 15:08.710
Ah! I think I've got
something that struck me

15:08.780 --> 15:09.850
as weird at the time.

15:09.950 --> 15:12.520
I, uh...
heard she liked sweets!

15:12.550 --> 15:15.990
I've got nothing.
Except maybe that--

15:16.020 --> 15:18.990
[EREN]
Guys. What are we doing?

15:19.020 --> 15:21.290
These are our comrades
we're talking about.

15:21.330 --> 15:23.860
Yeah, sure. Bertholdt
never has a lot to say.

15:23.960 --> 15:26.630
But Reiner's like everyone's
big brother, y'know?

15:26.670 --> 15:30.530
You really think
he's capable of lying to us?

15:30.570 --> 15:33.540
Eren does have a point.
Think about it.

15:33.570 --> 15:36.570
Reiner fought the Female Titan
with everything he had.

15:36.640 --> 15:40.310
Almost got himself squeezed to
a bloody pulp in the process.

15:40.350 --> 15:43.580
--[Gaspss]
--What's the matter?

15:43.650 --> 15:46.820
He burst free of her grip
at the last minute.

15:46.850 --> 15:50.020
Afterwards, though,
Annie changed her course.

15:50.060 --> 15:54.260
In fact, she ran straight
toward where you were.

15:54.330 --> 15:56.660
I-- I mentioned
that you might be

15:56.700 --> 15:57.830
rear of the center rank,

15:57.860 --> 16:00.160
but there's no way
she could've heard me.

16:00.200 --> 16:02.500
She wasn't in earshot
at the time.

16:02.530 --> 16:05.400
You've gotta be kidding.

16:05.440 --> 16:07.940
Do you recall if he seemed
unusually interested

16:08.010 --> 16:10.270
in Eren's location?

16:13.310 --> 16:18.250
So, where the hell
do you think he is?

16:18.280 --> 16:20.050
[ARMIN]
Oh, no.

16:23.420 --> 16:26.360
I only brought his position
up in the first place

16:26.390 --> 16:31.190
because Reiner asked me where
I thought Eren might be.

16:31.230 --> 16:34.560
Something else.
Once he broke free,

16:34.600 --> 16:37.300
the Female Titan stood
there staring at her palm,

16:37.370 --> 16:38.900
possibly transfixed
by something

16:38.940 --> 16:42.810
he'd carved onto it
with his blades.

16:42.880 --> 16:45.480
Maybe Reiner...

16:53.120 --> 16:55.250
What is wrong
with you people?

16:55.290 --> 16:57.620
The man's been with us
from the beginning!

16:57.660 --> 17:00.120
--You don't just--
--[HANGE] Enough!

17:00.160 --> 17:02.760
All of you. Listen up.

17:02.800 --> 17:05.160
If we cross paths
with the pair in question,

17:05.230 --> 17:08.630
don't give them any indication
of what we've discussed.

17:08.670 --> 17:10.430
And under no
circumstances are you

17:10.470 --> 17:13.340
to broach the topic of Annie
Leonhart in their company.

17:13.410 --> 17:16.640
Before we can ascertain whether
they were co-conspirators,

17:16.680 --> 17:20.080
we must find, lure,
and contain them underground.

17:20.110 --> 17:21.810
That's the plan. Are we clear?

17:21.850 --> 17:23.810
[SOLDIERS]
Yes, clear!

17:32.190 --> 17:35.430
You're just tired.
That's it, right?

17:35.460 --> 17:37.130
Help me out here, Betholdt.

17:37.160 --> 17:38.460
Your nerves are shot.

17:38.500 --> 17:40.600
You don't know
what you're saying.

17:40.630 --> 17:42.600
[BERTHOLDT]
Uh. Yeah.

17:42.670 --> 17:44.700
It's the battle fatigue talking!

17:44.770 --> 17:46.540
It's okay. You're okay.

17:46.610 --> 17:48.210
If you really were
the Armored Titan,

17:48.270 --> 17:50.170
what's the endgame here?

17:50.210 --> 17:53.680
We wouldn't be having this
conversation in the first place.

17:53.750 --> 17:56.050
What'd you expect
me to do? Say yes?

17:56.120 --> 18:00.620
Let myself be kidnaped just
'cause you asked politely?

18:00.650 --> 18:03.950
[REINER gasps]

18:10.730 --> 18:15.200
[REINER] Right.
Not thinking straight, am I?

18:15.230 --> 18:19.400
Barely know
what I'm saying here.

18:19.470 --> 18:22.170
Must've gone off the deep end.

18:25.140 --> 18:27.510
C'mon, let's go.

18:58.210 --> 19:01.080
[REINER]
That's the problem.

19:01.150 --> 19:03.780
Heh.

19:03.850 --> 19:07.720
I've been here too long
for my own good.

19:09.350 --> 19:15.430
Three years of this madness,
surrounded by idiots.

19:15.460 --> 19:21.430
We were kids. What'd we
know about anything?

19:21.470 --> 19:25.640
Why did there have to be
people like this?

19:25.700 --> 19:30.910
Why? Why did I
let myself devolve

19:30.940 --> 19:34.410
into such a half-assed
piece of shit?

19:36.280 --> 19:37.950
It's too late now.

19:37.980 --> 19:40.950
Damned if I know
what's right anymore!

19:40.990 --> 19:44.350
Who cares?
It is what it is.

19:44.390 --> 19:46.820
No choice but
to face what I've done.

19:46.890 --> 19:48.830
[BOTH gasp]

19:48.890 --> 19:51.230
As a warrior.

19:51.260 --> 19:55.230
No road left but the one
that leads to the end!

19:59.300 --> 20:01.510
Reiner! Right now?

20:01.570 --> 20:03.510
Here? We're doing this?

20:03.580 --> 20:06.280
Yes. Right here, right now!

20:06.310 --> 20:09.080
We settle this
once and for all!

20:11.420 --> 20:13.420
--[MIKASA grunts]
--[REINER groans]

20:13.450 --> 20:16.420
--[MIKASA grunts]
--[BERTHOLDT groans]

20:19.120 --> 20:20.860
[Groans]

20:20.930 --> 20:23.730
Eren! Get out of here!

20:26.130 --> 20:28.300
[REINER]
Bertholdt!

20:33.270 --> 20:36.940
Eren! Run away!

20:41.680 --> 20:43.180
[SASHA yells]

20:51.960 --> 20:55.790
[Growls]

21:13.350 --> 21:15.880
[Gasps]
Ymir!

21:20.690 --> 21:22.550
No!

21:35.030 --> 21:36.370
[REINER] I'm going
to return to the home

21:36.400 --> 21:38.600
that was taken from me.

21:38.670 --> 21:42.570
I will do it.
No matter what.

21:48.710 --> 21:52.650
[EREN]
Bertholdt. Reiner.

21:58.090 --> 22:02.630
[EREN]
Damn you! You traitors!

22:02.690 --> 22:06.460
[EREN TITAN yells]

22:09.640 --> 22:14.640
♪ Closing Song ♪
